WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.364 --> 00:00:20.325
ran toward the soccer goal, her feet dribbling the ball with perfect control.

2
00:00:23.646 --> 00:00:27.867
The scent of fresh-cut grass filled her nose as she sped forward.

3
00:00:29.107 --> 00:00:30.708
It gave her a burst of energy.

4
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.523
She faked to the right and then twisted her body left for a direct shot.

5
00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:44.429
Bam! The ball soared past the goalie's fingertips and into the net.

6
00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.732
"Score!" Jake high-fived Iris.

7
00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:54.235
His hand felt as hot and sweaty as her own.

8
00:00:55.957 --> 00:01:00.520
After all that running around, she hoped she didn't smell too terrible.

9
00:01:02.088 --> 00:01:08.830
"Yes!" Sophia jumped up and down at Iris' side, her dark ponytail bouncing with her.

10
00:01:11.151 --> 00:01:11.971
Iris grinned.

11
00:01:12.971 --> 00:01:15.052
The three of them made a great team.

12
00:01:16.372 --> 00:01:21.314
Now that seventh grade was over for the year, they were free to play soccer in the park

13
00:01:21.494 --> 00:01:23.334
every afternoon if they wanted to.

14
00:01:24.995 --> 00:01:29.656
No homework, no projects, no after-school activities.

15
00:01:31.304 --> 00:01:38.568
The best possible summer lay ahead, filled with many more sunny afternoons and soccer games like this one.

16
00:01:38.588 --> 00:01:41.290
"Game's over!"

17
00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:42.730
the goalie said.

18
00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.993
"You guys won today, but we'll beat you next week."

19
00:01:48.413 --> 00:01:49.274
"What time is it?"

20
00:01:49.774 --> 00:01:50.535
Jake asked.

21
00:01:51.535 --> 00:01:54.177
He patted his pockets, looking for his phone.

22
00:01:56.958 --> 00:01:58.019
But they were empty.

23
00:01:59.359 --> 00:02:00.180
Iris shrugged.

24
00:02:01.068 --> 00:02:05.231
The sun still hung above the treetops, so it couldn't be that late.

25
00:02:06.853 --> 00:02:12.477
She watched as Sophia jogged over to the sideline and dug through her soccer bag for her phone.

26
00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:18.782
Iris had told her friends that her mom wouldn't let her have a phone until high school.

27
00:02:19.963 --> 00:02:25.868
But the truth was, Mama couldn't afford phones for Iris and her twin brother, Javier.

28
00:02:27.548 --> 00:02:32.311
Mama could barely afford her own phone since Papa had left the family last year.

29
00:02:33.812 --> 00:02:38.474
Sometimes Iris missed Papa's shooting goals with her on Sunday mornings.

30
00:02:39.855 --> 00:02:43.417
Mostly, though, things were easier without him around.

31
00:02:44.758 --> 00:02:48.100
Across the field Sophia pulled her phone out of her bag.

32
00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.622
"It's six o'clock!"

33
00:02:52.622 --> 00:02:55.844
"Already?" Iris clapped a hand over her mouth.

34
00:02:56.684 --> 00:02:57.445
"I've got to go.

35
00:02:58.085 --> 00:02:59.206
Great game, everyone!"

36
00:02:59.747 --> 00:03:01.788
she yelled as she ran off the field.

37
00:03:01.808 --> 00:03:04.611
"See you tomorrow, Iris!"

38
00:03:05.391 --> 00:03:06.713
Sophia called after her.

39
00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:11.997
Without looking back, Iris waved and sped for home.

40
00:03:13.899 --> 00:03:18.182
Home for Iris was a brick apartment building two blocks from the park.

41
00:03:19.403 --> 00:03:23.707
Iris turned her key in the front lock and raced up to the third floor.

42
00:03:26.068 --> 00:03:33.231
She opened the door to her family's apartment as quietly as possible, but Javier had already spotted her.

43
00:03:34.632 --> 00:03:36.993
Her brother looked up from his computer screen.

44
00:03:37.013 --> 00:03:39.874
"You're late," he said.

45
00:03:41.034 --> 00:03:41.855
Iris scowled.

46
00:03:41.875 --> 00:03:48.498
"It's easier to get home on time if you're always here, playing with imaginary friends on the computer!"

47
00:03:50.298 --> 00:03:53.660
As usual, Javier was doing something online.

48
00:03:56.584 --> 00:04:00.605
This was why his skin was at least two shades lighter than hers.

49
00:04:02.006 --> 00:04:08.547
Other than that, the twins actually looked a lot alike, with the same dark eyes, full lips, and

50
00:04:08.687 --> 00:04:09.608
frizzy curls.

51
00:04:09.628 --> 00:04:14.529
"It's called gaming, not playing."

52
00:04:15.529 --> 00:04:17.210
Javier looked back at the screen.

53
00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.891
"Anyway, Mama's furious at you."

54
00:04:22.031 --> 00:04:25.472
Just then footsteps pounded down the hall from the kitchen.

55
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.460
"Iris? Are you here?"

56
00:04:30.101 --> 00:04:31.521
Mama's eyes blazed.

57
00:04:33.282 --> 00:04:35.922
"Finally! I was worried about you.

58
00:04:36.702 --> 00:04:39.003
Don't scare me like that again, young lady."

59
00:04:39.023 --> 00:04:43.044
"Mama, I was only ten minutes late."

60
00:04:44.164 --> 00:04:44.865
"No matter.

61
00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:51.847
This is why we have rules in this household, and this is why you're going to—" She pressed

62
00:04:51.907 --> 00:04:52.787
her lips together.

63
00:04:52.807 --> 00:04:55.067
"Never mind.

64
00:04:55.708 --> 00:04:56.988
I'll tell you more at dinner.

65
00:04:58.112 --> 00:04:59.353
Time to set the table."

66
00:05:00.614 --> 00:05:02.455
She thundered back down the hall.

67
00:05:07.319 --> 00:05:08.059
Iris whispered.

68
00:05:08.079 --> 00:05:10.221
"What was that about?"

69
00:05:11.042 --> 00:05:12.202
Javier shrugged.

70
00:05:12.222 --> 00:05:14.584
"I guess we'll find out."

71
00:05:15.745 --> 00:05:22.330
A few minutes later, the twins went into the kitchen, where the scents of cilantro, garlic, and tomato

72
00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.192
rose from a pot of beans simmering on the stove.

73
00:05:26.952 --> 00:05:32.195
Mama scooped rice into bowls, topping each with a big spoonful of beans.

74
00:05:33.656 --> 00:05:39.839
Javier poured water into tall glasses, and Iris got out forks and napkins.

75
00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:47.063
No one spoke, but Iris could hear their neighbor playing his flamenco guitar again.

76
00:05:48.664 --> 00:05:55.628
Listening to the music usually relaxed her quickly, but tonight she was nervous about what Mama had to

77
00:05:55.708 --> 00:05:59.993
say. Iris slipped into her seat.

78
00:06:01.114 --> 00:06:03.656
The three of them ate in silence for a few minutes.

79
00:06:07.298 --> 00:06:09.240
Finally Mama cleared her throat.

80
00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:13.403
"I have some news to share," she said.

81
00:06:13.423 --> 00:06:21.048
"I got a new job, and it's a good one, working full-time in an office as a receptionist."

82
00:06:22.769 --> 00:06:24.070
"That's great, Mama!"

83
00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:25.471
Javier said.

84
00:06:25.491 --> 00:06:29.858
"Yes." Iris nodded and smiled at her mother.

85
00:06:31.179 --> 00:06:35.842
A full-time job was just what Mama needed—and in an office!

86
00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:43.487
Mama had been getting by cleaning houses in the mornings, but she was smart and good with people.

87
00:06:45.068 --> 00:06:47.630
The office job sounded perfect for her.

88
00:06:49.131 --> 00:06:50.552
Mama's eyes sparkled.

89
00:06:50.572 --> 00:06:58.012
"I'll get to dress up for work instead of having to wear sloppy clothes and sneakers, and I'll

90
00:06:58.052 --> 00:06:59.813
have my own desk and computer.

91
00:07:00.713 --> 00:07:02.093
I can't wait to start."

92
00:07:04.074 --> 00:07:05.254
"When is your first day?"

93
00:07:06.034 --> 00:07:06.735
Iris asked.

94
00:07:06.755 --> 00:07:10.516
"That's the other thing I needed to tell you."

95
00:07:11.936 --> 00:07:13.456
Mama looked down at her bowl.

96
00:07:13.476 --> 00:07:18.258
"I start on Monday, and as I said, it's a full-time job.

97
00:07:19.718 --> 00:07:22.739
I can't leave the two of you here alone all day long."

98
00:07:22.759 --> 00:07:24.360
"Why not?"

99
00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:25.760
Iris frowned.

100
00:07:26.636 --> 00:07:28.197
"We're 13 years old."

101
00:07:28.217 --> 00:07:31.920
"Almost 14," Javier added.

102
00:07:33.861 --> 00:07:35.582
Mama waggled a finger at them.

103
00:07:35.602 --> 00:07:38.845
"Your birthday is not until November!

104
00:07:39.945 --> 00:07:43.648
Staying home alone for this much time is not up for discussion.

105
00:07:44.349 --> 00:07:47.351
Besides, I've already signed you up for a camp."

106
00:07:49.252 --> 00:07:51.714
"Camp?" Javier made a face.

107
00:07:52.975 --> 00:07:54.636
Iris smirked at Javier.

108
00:07:55.828 --> 00:07:58.349
"I guess you'll actually have to go outside this summer!"

109
00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:00.571
Then she looked at her mother.

110
00:08:00.591 --> 00:08:03.152
"What kind of camp is it, Mama?

111
00:08:03.752 --> 00:08:04.733
Soccer camp, I hope?"

112
00:08:06.194 --> 00:08:07.014
"I'm sorry."

113
00:08:07.814 --> 00:08:08.775
Mama shook her head.

114
00:08:08.795 --> 00:08:15.298
"With such late notice, the only camp that still had two openings was tennis camp."

115
00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.601
"Huh?" Javier's mouth dropped open.

116
00:08:20.621 --> 00:08:22.682
"Tennis camp?"

117
00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:25.484
Iris slumped back on her chair.

118
00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.842
She didn't know many kids who played tennis.

119
00:08:30.763 --> 00:08:33.765
Her friends mostly liked soccer and basketball.

120
00:08:34.886 --> 00:08:36.867
Mama's gaze flitted between them.

121
00:08:36.887 --> 00:08:39.209
"You're both very lucky.

122
00:08:39.229 --> 00:08:43.052
A lot of kids would love to attend a camp like this.

123
00:08:43.993 --> 00:08:45.914
I'm sure it'll be lots of fun."

124
00:08:47.775 --> 00:08:51.198
When Mama put it like that, they couldn't argue anymore.

125
00:08:52.239 --> 00:08:53.520
But tennis camp?

126
00:08:55.076 --> 00:08:57.518
Iris shared a worried glance with Javier.

127
00:08:58.538 --> 00:09:01.400
Javier hated outdoor sports, period.

128
00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:05.722
And she had zero interest in learning how to play tennis.

129
00:09:07.043 --> 00:09:12.026
Iris' "perfect" summer didn't seem so perfect anymore.
